imes adopts wrong tone, weak memory for numbers, makes nasty remarks. So indeed B has serious concerns. Candidate C: quick correct decisions, calm in crisis, technical competence, excellent attention, puts concern for others above everything. Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. So both have communication concerns. B's memory issue is more safety-critical. C's egocentric may affect crew cooperation but maybe less immediate.\n\nWe also have candidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Concerns: arrogant, weak leadership, hot temper, loner. Not as strong as C perhaps.\n\nCandidate A: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership, sometimes not good at taking criticism, can be unorganized. No data on stress resilience, memory, etc.\n\nThus C seems stronger overall. So we might shift to Candidate C. That aligns with Agent 2's recommendation. We need to reference Agent 2's points and maybe add our own perspective, maybe bring in a fact about C's concern for others (crew cooperation) and attention (attention skills). Also note that C's egocentric and communication difficulty are concerns but can be mitigated.\n\nThus we can change our vote to Candidate C.\n\nWe need to produce public message: \"I agree with Agent 2 that Candidate C is the stronger overall fit because...\" referencing evidence.\n\nWe must include metadata JSON with vote \"Candidate C\". Ensure correct format.\n\nProceed."}
